            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at 4U_Boutique Restaurant & Beer",
            "review_text": "LUVBALIBEACH\nSingapore793 contributions\n0\nLocal Restaurant near Han River\nSep 2019\nWe found this restaurant on our own. The hotel staff recommended one but it was too far so we walk and found this 100m from our hotel.\nIt had 2 story, level one had live seafood display so we chose to go level 2.\n\nDont expect too much from the staff who cannot speak or understand English.\nThe restaurant was practically empty with a 2 other group of customers. One group very drunk as they were speaking very loudly.\n\nWe were hungry so ordered local chili fish that tastes like our version of chili stingray. Fried chicken with fried rice. Chicken was good but rice bland. We feel that the local fried rice is tasteless. We had tried 2 more times at buffet setting.\n\nWe ordered a beef with vegetables dish and it was also good.\nTo top it we must have the local vietnam beer. It costs only sin$1.\nWe find it flat unlike most other beer we had tasted.\nHowever in Rome do what romans do....embracing local culture.\n\nWe need to call to get staff attention so this is not a good thing but we figure if you are there to eat. Thats fine.\n\nFor 2 persons, we paid about 500k dong, over sin $30 so this is not too bad\nWe did not order live seafood. I guess this is when not only fish get slaughtered but your wallet too. \n\nOverall the food was ok.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 13, 2019",
