            "review_text": "Luke W\n5 contributions\n0\nDo not eat here, 0 rating.\nApr 2019 • Couples\nStarted with a really nice host and manager who spoke good English who had to specially serve me and my girlfriend as no other waiters could speak a word of English. All down hill from there. \nWe went to eat upstairs but walked past sick on the stairs which looked to be from a group of 20 all drunk. After 5 minutes we decided to sit back downstairs and still the sick was not cleaned and numerous staff were just walking by it. We were then sat next to another group of drunk people.\nWe ordered 3 drinks but just 2 came, the bottled water did not come.\nI then ordered the beef steak, a lobster, and some fries. The fries did come. The beef steak was ok, overcooked and was a very small portion. The lobster on the other hand was not ok, the only fish on the 230gram lobster was the fish from the tail. The fish from under the ribs was completely missing from 1 half of the lobster which looked like it had fallen out when being cooked. \n\nAdditional to the very poor food, we were, what I can only describe as being violated by the staff and other customers. Of course because we are English we expect to have more attention than usual. However, to have 4 members of staff to literally be standing around our table staring at us while we ate, and laughing and commenting to each other (because we were using knife and folks and struggling to get into the poorly cooked lobster) is absolutely out of order for any culture. \nIf that is not bad enough, the drunk customers next to us had called over a waitress, began pointing at our table and laughing. The waitress then came over to the table, removed one of the glasses and moved a small bowl and plate closer infront of me while I was eating?!?!?!\n\nOverall food was very below average and not worth the 600k bill for 2 meals. \nStaff/service was embarrassingly poor. \nWorst meal I have ever been for in any country.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 11, 2019",
